      "A": "Research a sparse-obstacle exact algorithm: factorial/inverse-factorial binomials modulo MOD, coordinate-sort blocked cells plus destination, and inclusion-exclusion over reachable prior blocked cells. Define edge cases (blocked start/end, duplicates) and assess practical O(M²) limits; propose a hybrid threshold rather than assuming it always wins.",
      "B": "Research an exact dense-grid path DP replacement for the current O(n²) code: minimize allocation/cache costs and evaluate safe OpenMP wavefront or row-prefix-scan parallelization. Preserve modulo arithmetic and all blocked-cell semantics; focus on regimes where sparse inclusion-exclusion is unattractive.",
      "C": "Independently investigate a correctness-preserving hybrid strategy and any viable subquadratic sparse-point method or pruning/order optimization for the blocked-cell recurrence. Compare asymptotic and expected costs using the observed 0.07984 s baseline as the only performance datum; do not specialize to hidden inputs.",
